{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523108-backgrounds-like-domian-herd-etc-need-an-upgrade","id":1523108,"title":"Backgrounds like domian, herd, etc. need an upgrade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-24T17:48:40-07:00","id":1523108,"title":"Backgrounds like domian, herd, etc. need an upgrade","content":"When it comes to gameplay backgrounds like domain and herd are really only good for blood, and in most scenarios, blood is already trivially easy to attain and store. There should be a rule where your herd also acts as extremely loyal henchmen, and have domain give you modifiers to certain rolls such as streetwise, survival, or investigation.<br /> <br /> That's just what I think anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T20:50:18-07:00","id":1523116,"title":"","content":"Well, to be honest i kind of dropped the game around the time Revised came out, so i never once used the Domain - that always seemed like something of useless point sink, in a system where balance and value of each background can be already questionable in all editions.<br /> <br /> I only got curious about Masquerade again around the time Beckett's Jyhad Diary came out and very recently - a month or two, three months tops - started STing a chronicle with lots of over-the-top inspiration on Bloodlines, Redemption, the Winter's Teeth V5 comic alongside some obscure metaplot events and a timeline tweak here &amp; there. Rules-wise, i use V20 with some adjustments to disciplines and backgrounds (that i kind of subsumed some merits, flaws and V5's concept of loresheets into).<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> Herd i still use, but have tinkered it somewhat to my own table in that beside the bonus to hunting or one's blood pool, the character also gets a number of &quot;basic&quot; ghouls at one's beck and call (their polls already mostly accounted in herd upkeep &amp; etc), with the possiblity of tweaks like a herd with smaller number of somewhat supernatural people like thin-bloods or revenants.<br /> <br /> (Ironically, only PC to actually get a Herd in the group is a Caitiff - though due to social skills, fame and attitude, a lot of people confuse him for Toreador or Malkavian)<br /> <br /> <br /> Retainers i reserve for &quot;special&quot; ghouls - aka, probably <b>much</b> older than the PC itself (like retainer level = age tier) and that were obtained through favor from a patron, trickery, luck or who knows what weird reasons.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-24-2023, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T03:32:22-07:00","id":1523167,"title":"","content":"Backgrounds and I have a love/hate relationship.<br /> <br /> I love how they can be adjusted by play rather than by XP and that often what they are capable of is more than just the sum of their parts. On the other hand, I hate the fact that the game system as a whole seems to have a collective melt down when a player leverages Backgrounds in a way that isn't just handwaving the bookkeeping.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would love there to be an expansion book that adds depth to the Backgrounds, in the same way the Exalted 2nd Edition Oadenol's Codex book created whole new aspects of play just by adding depth to the Manse background. You are free to use the simple Background found in the core book for faster character creation or you can use the expanded rules for far more intricate use of the background.<br /> <br /> Domain suffers from being so abstract that it is bent into whatever a given game needs rather than having its own mechanics. For example, if your domain is a local hospital, the rating could mean that you are an orderly who practically lives there and considers it their personal hunting grounds or personal plot point area (Being Human). Alternatively, Domain could mean that the hospital is owned by you, meaning that it gives you a Resources score, its blood bank counts as a Herd score, the fact that you can get off the books medical work done gives you Influence and Status scores not to mention an Ally score.<br /> <br /> There comes a point where having a high enough Resources ranking means that you start &quot;buying&quot; background dots which in turn magnify your ability to acquire Resources, but since Rank 5 is as high as you can go in the system, you have to start upgrading your Coterie mates Resources to take advantage of Pooled Backgrounds, but with little effort you can max out all of them. What exactly does game balance look like when the coterie has a Resources 25 ranking? Your coterie GDP and Influence levels is greater than most nations and that can be generated by starting character grade stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T10:53:34-07:00","id":1523222,"title":"","content":"So Baaldam was the Caitiff every found out by the rest of Kindred society of being a clan imposter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T22:42:22-07:00","id":1523256,"title":"","content":"Backgrounds should be something gained or lost continually.<br /> <br /> Every vampire in the city is looking for safe blood, and an edge over their competition. Every hunt is dangerous. It represents exposure, it represents the prospect of hunters, law enforcement, or some idiot with a cell phone camera recording them. It represents possibly stepping on the toes of other vampires who are also hunting, or worse, protecting THEIR herd.<br /> <br /> That Domain 2, Resources 3, and Herd 3 that your Strip Club Haven represents is a tempting target for that Ventrue ancilla with a childe. What do you do when some starving Brujah douchebag wants to feed from a stripper - a member of your Herd? What if YOU are that Brujah douchebag? Or that Ventrue?<br /> <br /> You want Backgrounds to mean something, then make them mean something. A vampire with no Backgrounds has no money, no safe haven, no influence, nobody to help them out. Every hunt should be an upward slog, every daylight hour a threat. A vampire with tons of Backgrounds should feel like they're on Easy Street. Resources, mansions, free blood, constant streams of intel, and lackeys to do the dirty work are all on the table. Give them the Golden Spoon, then threaten to take it away. This is what makes Elders so cagey and paranoid about their interests anyway, let your group get a taste of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27252,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","user":"Hades","date":". 09-28-2023, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T01:20:11-07:00","id":1523263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523108-backgrounds-like-domian-herd-etc-need-an-upgrade?p=1523256#post1523256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backgrounds should be something gained or lost continually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Backgrounds should be very dynamic compared to the rest of the mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523108-backgrounds-like-domian-herd-etc-need-an-upgrade?p=1523256#post1523256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every vampire in the city is looking for safe blood, and an edge over their competition. Every hunt is dangerous. It represents exposure, it represents the prospect of hunters, law enforcement, or some idiot with a cell phone camera recording them. It represents possibly stepping on the toes of other vampires who are also hunting, or worse, protecting THEIR herd.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those things that is both a game style and to a certain extent a home brew issue.<br /> <br /> We have vampire population ratios that explicitly state that the largest cities in the world would have between 6 to 12 vampires in them, not even enough to have a full council and have cainites to rule over. So, stepping on other vampire's toes is practically a plot point rather than a tactical misstep.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I have messed around with making feeding more or less problematic with different stories to see how it affects the game and it is more of a flavor than a hard mechanical adjustment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523108-backgrounds-like-domian-herd-etc-need-an-upgrade?p=1523256#post1523256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want Backgrounds to mean something, then make them mean something. A vampire with no Backgrounds has no money, no safe haven, no influence, nobody to help them out. Every hunt should be an upward slog, every daylight hour a threat. A vampire with tons of Backgrounds should feel like they're on Easy Street. Resources, mansions, free blood, constant streams of intel, and lackeys to do the dirty work are all on the table. Give them the Golden Spoon, then threaten to take it away. This is what makes Elders so cagey and paranoid about their interests anyway, let your group get a taste of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely with the carrot and stick approach to poking at the PCs backgrounds, but in practice I have always found that even if you destroy their Background pools completely, they can be built back up with remarkable speed.<br /> <br /> A &quot;Boon Generator&quot; build character can speed run the acquisition of Backgrounds and Boons to the point where almost every game causes a jump in stats. Yes the ST can poke at them a bit to retard progression, but after a certain point it becomes farcical that every elder is personally knocking down your attempts to buy property, meet people, or help out other local kindred, especially when as I said before there is unlikely to be more than half a dozen vampires total in the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T06:39:56-07:00","id":1523304,"title":"","content":"If you want a handwave-y but quick &quot;boost&quot; to Backgrounds, let players add them to relevant dice pools, and apply them liberally.<br /> <br /> Domain might add to dice pools to remain hidden in a large hunting ground, or the ST might use those dots as a penalty for an intruder who wants to avoid your traps.<br /> <br /> While Retainers gives you well trained ghouls, Herd gives you weak nooks to throw in the path of others. A herd might also give you access to information, or a bonus to Intimidation or Status-related actions where having numbers on your side would help. Your herd might also be able to provide you with a safe house at a time of crisis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T15:37:31-07:00","id":1523577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523108-backgrounds-like-domian-herd-etc-need-an-upgrade#post1523108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to gameplay backgrounds like domain and herd are really only good for blood, and in most scenarios, blood is already trivially easy to attain and store. There should be a rule where your herd also acts as extremely loyal henchmen, and have domain give you modifiers to certain rolls such as streetwise, survival, or investigation.<br /> <br /> That's just what I think anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would be nice.<br /> <br /> In practice, Backgrounds are as useful or as useless as the Storyteller chooses to make them.<br /> <br /> Frankly, the &quot;gathering dots&quot; system sucks for Backgrounds anyway.<br /> <br /> Merits are so much better, because they tend to be well defined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27548-vanceonice","name":"VanceOnIce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T10:48:18-07:00","id":1523724,"title":"","content":"Actually i dont think the backgrounds in themselves need a boost ! Ressources is great ... but having a safe haven, status, a herd and a powerful mentor backing you are even higher vital priorities ! What does need a major boost however is examples of how all that stuff as well as boons, domain and influence intertwines with the setting and the stories. These things are mentionned to be central to the game, but i have always felt they were under used in the game systems and lore as opposed to disciplines. Ww tried to add mechanics to domain in v5, but i think it was \u00e0 pretty weak try. Something like backgrounds fluidly feeding into eachother and bumping into other cainite's reach when they get high could be something to work on. That and actual plots about prestation influence and domain and how those notions can become contradictive ie : one dude has official domain over something, another has actual influence and another Guy uses favors to get something in that area done. The result ? A big mess and a good plot !!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28217-remithemonkey","name":"remithemonkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T13:48:52-08:00","id":1525478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523108-backgrounds-like-domian-herd-etc-need-an-upgrade?p=1523222#post1523222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Baaldam was the Caitiff every found out by the rest of Kindred society of being a clan imposter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's the funny part - he is not an imposter. If asked about actual lineage and origin he has no issue in admiting he's one of the clanless. But fame due to his Lestat-esque stage persona precedes him, ergo people make assumptions on their own and only rarely actually ask.<br /> <br /> Yes, he's a walking Masquerade affront, but is far from the only one and his wandering existence combined with some well-placed associates &amp; acquaintances here and there go a long way toward his continued existence.<br /> <br /> Being the unauthorized impulse embrace childe of an archon can have some very interesting ups &amp; downs for one's unlife - combine that with belonging to a noddist cult....<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T15:53:49-08:00","id":1525487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523108-backgrounds-like-domian-herd-etc-need-an-upgrade#post1523108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to gameplay backgrounds like domain and herd are really only good for blood, and in most scenarios, blood is already trivially easy to attain and store. There should be a rule where your herd also acts as extremely loyal henchmen, and have domain give you modifiers to certain rolls such as streetwise, survival, or investigation.<br /> <br /> That's just what I think anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a player who is a Toreador burlesque artist, and they moved part of their campaign from Vhicago to Aspen for a while and as Aspen is not too big and the Prince there do not like too much feeding, the Toreador invited and paid for a flight + hotel to Aspen for his Herd (who are fans to his show) and as he has fame 2, the herd felt special and after a good roll he managed to get the herd to go on a 2-week vacation in the winter to Aspen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T01:45:01-08:00","id":1525503,"title":"","content":"In 1e &amp; 2e Herd apart from being a blood supply was also the lowest level of Minion,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28255-dropbear","name":"DropBear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}